<div class="space-y-6">
  <div>
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">Announcements</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-4">
    
    <div class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm border border-base-300">
      <div class="card-body space-y-3">
        <h2 class="card-title text-base font-bold">Streaming & AI Platform Unlock Detection Online</h2>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-base-content/60 bg-base-200/50 w-fit px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md">
          <span>Published on 2026/9/5 12:34:21</span>
        </div>
        <div class="divider my-0"></div>
        <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
          You can now check the unlock status of mainstream AI and streaming platforms for each node in the node status page, automatically checked every 10 minutes; at the same time, we have expanded the traffic detail charts to 31 days, but currently only data from the 17th onwards can be queried, and data will slowly fill up until 31 days are complete.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card bg-base-100 shadow-sm border border-base-300">
      <div class="card-body space-y-3">
        <h2 class="card-title text-base font-bold">Traffic Details Expansion</h2>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-base-content/60 bg-base-200/50 w-fit px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md">
          <span>Published on 2026/8/25 15:28:47</span>
        </div>
        <div class="divider my-0"></div>
        <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            To further enhance the query experience and visualization capabilities of traffic data, we have completed the overall restructuring and upgrade of the traffic details feature.
          </p>
          <p>
            After this upgrade, the traffic usage view has been expanded to the last 14 days. You can view traffic usage within the last 14 days with a data statistics granularity of 5 minutes, allowing a more intuitive and detailed understanding of traffic changes across different time periods.
          </p>
          <p>
            Due to this upgrade involving the expansion of data storage and statistical capabilities, historical traffic data can currently be queried starting from August 15, so traffic usage records before August 15 cannot be viewed.
          </p>
          <p>
            We will continue to monitor system operation, query load, and resource usage, and further expand the visual query range to 31 days based on actual conditions.
          </p>
          <p>
            Thank you for your understanding and support; we will continue to optimize the service experience and data capabilities.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>